-- title:
--   Local invariant of χsmileκₐ equals χ(Frob) v_q(a)
-- statement:
--   Fix primes $p$ and $q$, a primitive $p$-th root of unity $\zeta$ in $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, and write $G_q$ for the group of $\mathbb{Q}_q$-algebra automorphisms of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}_q$ (`PadicAlgCl q`). Let $u$ be a unit of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}_q$ whose underlying element is the image of $\zeta$ under the fixed embedding [`padicEmbedding q`](def/GaloisRep_CompletionBridge.html#L17) of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ into $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}_q$. Let $\chi\colon G_q\to\mathbb{Z}$ be level constant with respect to [`localGaloisToGlobal q`](def/GaloisRep_CompletionBridge.html#L41) (restriction of scalars to $\mathbb{Q}$, followed by restriction to $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$), satisfy $p\mid\chi\sigma+\chi\tau-\chi(\sigma\tau)$ for all $\sigma,\tau$, and satisfy, for every $\sigma$, that $\sigma$ fixes every $x$ with $x^{q^p-1}=1$ if and only if $p\mid\chi\sigma$. Let $\varphi\in G_q$ act by $x\mapsto x^q$ on all such $x$. Let $a$ be a unit of $\mathbb{Q}_q$ and $\alpha$ a unit of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}_q$ with $a=\alpha^p$ in $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}_q$. Let $z\colon G_q\times G_q\to\mathbb{Z}/p$ lie in `levelCocycles₂` for the representation `ofChar` attached to the mod-$p$ cyclotomic character composed with `primeLocalToGlobal q`, i.e. $\mathbb{Z}/p$ with the Galois action twisted by that character. Assume finally that the $2$-cochain $g\mapsto u^{(z\,g).\mathrm{val}}$, written additively, differs from $g\mapsto g_1\bigl(\kappa_\alpha(g_2)\bigr)^{\chi(g_1)}$ — where $\kappa_\alpha(\sigma)=\sigma\alpha/\alpha\in\mu_p$ is the Kummer cocycle of $\alpha$, pushed into $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}_q^\times$ — by an element of `levelCoboundaries₂` for the action of $G_q$ on $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}_q^\times$. Then the pinned local invariant `localInv p ζ q` (the unique $\mathbb{Z}/p$-linear functional on the level-continuous $H^2$ satisfying `IsLocalInv`, and $0$ if no such unique functional exists), evaluated on the class of $z$ under `continuousH2π`, equals $\chi(\varphi)$ times the $q$-adic valuation of $a$, both read in $\mathbb{Z}/p$.
--
--   This is the evaluation of the norm-residue symbol of an unramified character of order $p$ over $\mathbb{Q}_q$: the local invariant of the cup product of $\bar\chi$ with the Kummer class of $a$ is $\chi(\mathrm{Frob})\cdot v_q(a)$, here transported to the normalisation of `localInv` fixed by the unramified degree-$p$ extension generated by the $(q^p-1)$-st roots of unity, arithmetic Frobenius and uniformiser $q$. It is used by [`PadicAlgCl.dvd_valuation_of_smul_kummerCocycle_pairing_mem_levelCoboundaries2`](thm.html#PadicAlgCl.dvd_valuation_of_smul_kummerCocycle_pairing_mem_levelCoboundaries2) to convert vanishing of the local invariant into a divisibility statement for valuations.
